1
00:00:00,549 --> 00:00:02,092
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:04,219 --> 00:00:05,762
[Taiki] Mom, where's my towel?

3
00:00:05,846 --> 00:00:07,431
[Yukiko] I left it out for you.

4
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:09,182
Found it.

5
00:00:09,266 --> 00:00:10,475
Of course you did.

6
00:00:11,101 --> 00:00:12,185
You're right, sorry.

7
00:00:13,979 --> 00:00:14,938
[gasps]

8
00:00:17,023 --> 00:00:18,942
{\an8}TAIKI - CHINATSU
PREFECTURAL QUALIFIERS

9
00:00:24,114 --> 00:00:26,116
[opening theme song playing]

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,454
BLUE BOX

11
00:01:46,613 --> 00:01:52,953
BLUE BOX

12
00:01:53,036 --> 00:01:54,996
EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

13
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,998
EPISODE 7
CAN I HAVE ONE?

14
00:02:03,588 --> 00:02:04,756
[grunts]

15
00:02:09,511 --> 00:02:12,264
- And it's Haryu for the win again!
- [grunts]

16
00:02:13,265 --> 00:02:14,766
I demand a rematch!

17
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:16,768
No, thanks, dude.

18
00:02:16,852 --> 00:02:19,187
[Taiki groans] Just one more, come on.

19
00:02:19,271 --> 00:02:21,022
[Haryu] I mean, if you like losing.

20
00:02:22,649 --> 00:02:24,442
If you get used to losing to me,

21
00:02:24,526 --> 00:02:26,778
you'll probably lose to me
at the tournament, too.

22
00:02:27,571 --> 00:02:29,781
Maybe that's your own self-doubt talking.

23
00:02:30,407 --> 00:02:31,867
You know, since you just can't seem

24
00:02:31,950 --> 00:02:33,785
- to win a match against Hyodo?
- [grunts]

25
00:02:34,452 --> 00:02:36,329
[Nishida] <i>Yeah,
and after the last tournament,</i>

26
00:02:36,413 --> 00:02:39,291
{\an8}<i>you got third in the prefecture,
and he took it all at nationals!</i>

27
00:02:39,374 --> 00:02:40,792
[in a scary voice] What was that?

28
00:02:40,876 --> 00:02:41,960
Okay, let's rally.

29
00:02:42,043 --> 00:02:43,295
It's about that time.

30
00:02:43,879 --> 00:02:44,963
[Haryu grunts softly]

31
00:02:45,046 --> 00:02:48,383
Anyway, I've got a laundry list of things
I wanna work on,

32
00:02:48,466 --> 00:02:50,677
so you're on your own for practice.

33
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,761
[exclaims softly]

34
00:02:53,263 --> 00:02:57,058
We may be doubles partners,
but we're opponents in singles.

35
00:02:57,142 --> 00:02:58,268
[gasps]

36
00:02:59,728 --> 00:03:00,812
You're right.

37
00:03:01,396 --> 00:03:03,815
From now on,
I aim all my smashes at your crotch.

38
00:03:03,899 --> 00:03:05,317
What?!

39
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,360
[Nagisa] I thought
we were gonna make that pass.

40
00:03:07,444 --> 00:03:08,320
- [Haryu] Oh.
- Huh?

41
00:03:08,403 --> 00:03:09,738
Hey, good hustle.

42
00:03:09,821 --> 00:03:11,156
Yeah, good hustle.

43
00:03:11,239 --> 00:03:12,324
Same to you.

44
00:03:13,033 --> 00:03:15,243
Practices been exhausting lately?

45
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:17,329
[Nagisa sighs]
We have a tournament coming up.

46
00:03:17,913 --> 00:03:19,748
Plus it's not just about us,

47
00:03:19,831 --> 00:03:22,584
we wanna make sure
our upperclassmen get to nationals.

48
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:23,877
Whoa.

49
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,170
That's big of you.

50
00:03:25,253 --> 00:03:28,590
[Taiki] <i>I bet this guy's never had
a thought like that in his life.</i>

51
00:03:29,424 --> 00:03:31,343
When do the girls' qualifiers start?

52
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:33,428
[Taiki] <i>Next Saturday.</i>

53
00:03:33,511 --> 00:03:35,972
[Nagisa] Next Saturday.
What about badminton?

54
00:03:36,056 --> 00:03:38,308
Yours are on the 18th, right?

55
00:03:38,391 --> 00:03:40,227
Hang on, how did you know that?

56
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:42,520
[Chinatsu] It was
in the school's newsletter.

57
00:03:42,604 --> 00:03:44,397
[Nagisa] I didn't know anyone read those.

58
00:03:44,481 --> 00:03:45,732
[Chinatsu] They're interesting.

59
00:03:45,815 --> 00:03:47,984
The principal writes
satirical poems sometimes.

60
00:03:48,068 --> 00:03:50,654
[Nagisa laughs]
That's a segment in the newsletter?

61
00:03:50,737 --> 00:03:52,489
[Taiki] <i>I wonder if Chinatsu...</i>

62
00:03:52,572 --> 00:03:57,077
<i>is keeping an eye...
on when my tournament is, too.</i>

63
00:04:02,082 --> 00:04:05,001
SHOPPING DISTRICT

64
00:04:06,169 --> 00:04:08,505
[Taiki] <i>Ten more days till qualifiers.</i>

65
00:04:08,588 --> 00:04:11,049
<i>Like Haryu said, I'm on my own</i>

66
00:04:11,132 --> 00:04:14,052
<i>to fine tune everything I can
between now and then.</i>

67
00:04:15,679 --> 00:04:17,681
[groans]

68
00:04:17,764 --> 00:04:21,017
<i>Why didn't I start working
on my backhand drive sooner?</i>

69
00:04:21,101 --> 00:04:22,519
{\an8}LAST-MINUTE REGRETS

70
00:04:23,853 --> 00:04:24,771
[gasps]

71
00:04:25,981 --> 00:04:26,856
<i>Chinatsu.</i>

72
00:04:29,109 --> 00:04:30,777
<i>She's carrying a lot of stuff.</i>

73
00:04:32,028 --> 00:04:33,196
<i>Should I help her?</i>

74
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,364
I'll help you!

75
00:04:34,447 --> 00:04:36,074
Oh, really? Are you sure?

76
00:04:36,157 --> 00:04:36,992
<i>But...</i>

77
00:04:37,617 --> 00:04:39,369
What if someone were to see us?

78
00:04:39,869 --> 00:04:41,079
[groans]

79
00:04:41,162 --> 00:04:42,330
Think she's a high schooler?

80
00:04:42,414 --> 00:04:44,541
- Yeah she's really cute.
- [Taiki exclaims]

81
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,420
Let me help carry those.

82
00:04:48,503 --> 00:04:49,546
Wait, Taiki?

83
00:04:50,463 --> 00:04:52,674
No, don't worry,
it's nothing I can't handle.

84
00:04:52,757 --> 00:04:55,302
Plus you gotta be exhausted
from practice, too.

85
00:04:55,927 --> 00:05:00,223
And anyway, you said walking home
with a girl would be uncomfortable right?

86
00:05:00,307 --> 00:05:01,266
Well, I...

87
00:05:03,435 --> 00:05:05,186
All right, time for take two.

88
00:05:08,189 --> 00:05:11,568
Oh, aren't you Chinatsu
from the basketball team?

89
00:05:12,444 --> 00:05:14,529
What are the odds, running into you here?

90
00:05:15,113 --> 00:05:16,865
Do you live around here, perchance?

91
00:05:16,948 --> 00:05:19,409
I live in a neighborhood
not far from here!

92
00:05:19,492 --> 00:05:21,536
Looks like you could use some help.

93
00:05:21,619 --> 00:05:22,871
I'll carry them.

94
00:05:22,954 --> 00:05:24,080
Strength training.

95
00:05:24,706 --> 00:05:25,540
Onward!

96
00:05:25,623 --> 00:05:27,584
SPECIAL TECHNIQUE:
CHANCE MEETING ON THE WAY HOME

97
00:05:29,002 --> 00:05:30,545
[chuckles] What are you doing?

98
00:05:35,425 --> 00:05:37,594
[Chinatsu] So you live this way, too, huh?

99
00:05:37,677 --> 00:05:40,096
[Taiki] I know, right? What a kawinkidink?

100
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,681
[Chinatsu] What a kawinkidink.

101
00:05:42,223 --> 00:05:44,601
[Taiki] Fun fact,
I live in a two-story house.

102
00:05:44,684 --> 00:05:46,019
Hey, I do, too.

103
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:48,521
And there's a chiropractor nearby.

104
00:05:48,605 --> 00:05:49,856
I know where that is.

105
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:53,860
What's crazy is that I've only been living
at my current place since March.

106
00:05:54,694 --> 00:05:56,529
And so how has it been living there?

107
00:05:56,613 --> 00:05:58,114
Oh, it's been so great!

108
00:05:58,198 --> 00:06:00,408
Everyone has been really sweet and kind.

109
00:06:00,492 --> 00:06:02,619
The whole family
has been incredibly welcoming.

110
00:06:03,286 --> 00:06:05,038
Sweet and kind?

111
00:06:05,121 --> 00:06:07,248
You left a tissue in your pocket again.

112
00:06:07,332 --> 00:06:10,627
Get some strength training in
and gimme a massage, would ya?

113
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:14,923
Thanks to all of them, I can keep pursuing
my dream that I almost gave up on.

114
00:06:15,006 --> 00:06:17,467
[pleasant music playing]

115
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:19,511
I'm glad I moved into that house.

116
00:06:24,224 --> 00:06:25,433
Chinatsu.

117
00:06:25,517 --> 00:06:27,644
Rock-paper-scissors, shoot!

118
00:06:29,354 --> 00:06:31,397
- Yes! I win.
- [groans]

119
00:06:32,607 --> 00:06:34,943
I know you're super tired and everything,

120
00:06:35,026 --> 00:06:37,028
but can you come with me for a sec?

121
00:06:37,695 --> 00:06:39,989
- Huh?
- It's around the corner.

122
00:06:50,125 --> 00:06:51,042
OYASU SHRINE

123
00:06:51,126 --> 00:06:54,587
[Taiki] For years, I've visited here
the day before I have something big.

124
00:06:54,671 --> 00:06:56,131
[Chinatsu] Wow, a shrine?

125
00:06:56,214 --> 00:06:57,799
PRAYER FOR VICTORY

126
00:07:00,468 --> 00:07:02,303
Let's go up and pray for victory.

127
00:07:03,138 --> 00:07:05,056
I never knew there was a shrine here.

128
00:07:05,849 --> 00:07:08,810
And in the summer,
it's a great place to catch beetles.

129
00:07:08,893 --> 00:07:10,687
Bugs... scare me.

130
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:26,953
[Taiki] <i>Chinatsu decided to live
in another person's house</i>

131
00:07:27,036 --> 00:07:30,373
<i>just so she could pursue
her dream of going to nationals.</i>

132
00:07:31,458 --> 00:07:33,251
<i>I have no ulterior motive.</i>

133
00:07:33,793 --> 00:07:36,337
<i>I just want this for her as a peer.</i>

134
00:07:41,593 --> 00:07:48,224
<i>Please... please... I pray for both
Chinatsu and I to make it to nationals.</i>

135
00:07:52,437 --> 00:07:54,355
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

136
00:07:55,190 --> 00:07:57,358
Set up a net in the back court, too.

137
00:07:57,442 --> 00:08:00,236
[boy] Oh. Are you sure?
What about the other clubs?

138
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,613
Don't worry, it's fine.

139
00:08:02,238 --> 00:08:03,364
[Taiki] <i>Oh. Right.</i>

140
00:08:04,616 --> 00:08:07,202
<i>The basketball team's tournament
starts today.</i>

141
00:08:07,952 --> 00:08:09,162
[girl] You got it!

142
00:08:09,245 --> 00:08:11,372
[all cheering]

143
00:08:13,208 --> 00:08:14,250
[spectators] Eimei!

144
00:08:14,334 --> 00:08:15,418
Eimei!

145
00:08:15,502 --> 00:08:17,462
Eimei! Eimei!

146
00:08:17,545 --> 00:08:18,379
Natsu!

147
00:08:19,714 --> 00:08:21,132
[motivational music playing]

148
00:08:33,228 --> 00:08:35,146
[whistle blows]

149
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:38,650
[referee] 78 to 54.
Eimei High School takes it!

150
00:08:39,901 --> 00:08:41,444
- Let's go!
- Yeah!

151
00:08:42,195 --> 00:08:43,780
[crying]

152
00:08:45,532 --> 00:08:47,408
Nice job, Chinatsu!

153
00:08:47,492 --> 00:08:49,244
Tickle, tickle, tickle...

154
00:08:49,327 --> 00:08:51,704
Quit it, Nagisa. I am super sweaty.

155
00:08:51,788 --> 00:08:54,040
Oh, no, but it's a victory tickle!

156
00:08:54,123 --> 00:08:57,418
Nagi, don't get carried away.

157
00:08:57,502 --> 00:08:59,671
The qualifiers only just started.

158
00:08:59,754 --> 00:09:01,673
Ah, just lemme do my thing.

159
00:09:01,756 --> 00:09:04,300
Why don't I tickle you, too?
I mean, if we're gonna get hyped,

160
00:09:04,384 --> 00:09:07,512
we might as well take advantage
and go all out, right?

161
00:09:07,595 --> 00:09:11,558
Well, every team has a goofball,
and I'm glad ours is you.

162
00:09:11,641 --> 00:09:13,560
- Ah, well.
- [whistle blows]

163
00:09:13,643 --> 00:09:16,604
- [all cheering]
- Looks like they won their game, too.

164
00:09:16,688 --> 00:09:19,357
[Gomi] Guess we'll be facing
Kagohara Academy

165
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,775
in the finals again, huh?

166
00:09:22,819 --> 00:09:25,071
We gotta take our revenge after last year.

167
00:09:29,409 --> 00:09:30,702
Chinatsu.

168
00:09:30,785 --> 00:09:32,787
Hello, you're zoned out.

169
00:09:33,621 --> 00:09:35,123
I just really wanna win.

170
00:09:35,665 --> 00:09:39,252
[chuckles] So show it on your face,
then, 'cause that's not it.

171
00:09:39,919 --> 00:09:42,213
[Chinatsu] Show... what on my face?

172
00:09:46,426 --> 00:09:48,553
[coach] We'll be heading back
to school shortly.

173
00:09:48,636 --> 00:09:50,305
Meet by the bus in ten, yes?

174
00:09:50,388 --> 00:09:51,347
[girls] Yes!

175
00:09:52,098 --> 00:09:53,933
- Let's hit the bathroom.
- Mm.

176
00:09:55,351 --> 00:09:58,605
And when we had that shot,
it had to be a three or bust, so then...

177
00:09:58,688 --> 00:09:59,606
Ah...

178
00:10:01,941 --> 00:10:02,775
{\an8}KAGOHARA ACADEMY

179
00:10:02,859 --> 00:10:04,027
{\an8}[Nagisa] It's Kagohara...

180
00:10:05,153 --> 00:10:07,530
[Kagohara player]
Is this the match that Eimei just played?

181
00:10:07,614 --> 00:10:09,991
So then, number ten is gonna be Kano.

182
00:10:10,575 --> 00:10:12,368
There's nothing special about her.

183
00:10:14,537 --> 00:10:18,082
I got the impression she's no better
since the last practice match.

184
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:20,877
As long as I stay on her,
she won't be a problem.

185
00:10:21,586 --> 00:10:23,421
It's honestly pretty disappointing.

186
00:10:23,504 --> 00:10:25,048
- Uh...
- Nagisa.

187
00:10:26,674 --> 00:10:27,634
Let's go.

188
00:10:27,717 --> 00:10:29,010
Uh, but...

189
00:10:29,093 --> 00:10:33,097
It's totally normal Kagohara would be
researching their potential opponents,

190
00:10:33,181 --> 00:10:36,142
and the conclusions they draw from that
are really none of our business.

191
00:10:36,225 --> 00:10:37,769
I've seen you watch the pro league,

192
00:10:37,852 --> 00:10:40,188
and you seem comfortable
saying whatever you want.

193
00:10:40,271 --> 00:10:41,147
[groans]

194
00:10:41,814 --> 00:10:42,732
Come on.

195
00:10:45,193 --> 00:10:46,361
[sighs]

196
00:10:47,236 --> 00:10:49,656
LET'S GO TO NATIONALS
BADMINTON TEAM - TENNIS TEAM

197
00:10:49,739 --> 00:10:51,699
[grunts]

198
00:10:52,492 --> 00:10:56,663
- 21 to 14 and 21 to 13. Haryu wins.
- [panting]

199
00:10:58,790 --> 00:11:00,124
What a bummer, dude.

200
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:03,503
I'm undefeated with 13 wins this month.

201
00:11:04,128 --> 00:11:05,421
Thanks for the warm-up.

202
00:11:06,255 --> 00:11:08,216
[Taiki] <i>Man,
if I could beat him just once,</i>

203
00:11:08,299 --> 00:11:09,926
<i>before the tournament starts.</i>

204
00:11:12,512 --> 00:11:17,266
<i>I need to focus on my footwork.
And how dare he call me a "warm-up"?</i>

205
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:19,936
- [Kikuchi] We're starting right away.
- [girls] Yes!

206
00:11:20,019 --> 00:11:22,063
[Taiki] <i>Girls' basketball is back.</i>

207
00:11:22,146 --> 00:11:25,108
Their game was earlier,
so I guess they're back to practice.

208
00:11:25,191 --> 00:11:26,317
I guess you're right.

209
00:11:29,070 --> 00:11:30,613
They won, didn't they?

210
00:11:30,696 --> 00:11:32,573
Uh-huh, that's what the girls said.

211
00:11:33,199 --> 00:11:36,119
You'd think that they would look
more excited about it.

212
00:11:41,249 --> 00:11:45,336
<i>Then again, they can't really relax
until nationals are over.</i>

213
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:47,922
[Nagisa] If I were Chinatsu,
I'd be furious.

214
00:11:48,548 --> 00:11:49,841
[Taiki] <i>Her teammates.</i>

215
00:11:49,924 --> 00:11:52,009
To think they'd say she's nothing special,

216
00:11:52,093 --> 00:11:54,512
or hasn't gotten better,
from just watching one clip?

217
00:11:54,595 --> 00:11:57,390
Well, you can't go complaining
about every little comment you hear.

218
00:11:57,473 --> 00:11:58,850
Yeah, I know that, but...

219
00:11:58,933 --> 00:12:01,102
I think about her living situation.

220
00:12:01,727 --> 00:12:03,104
We all know about it.

221
00:12:04,021 --> 00:12:05,440
She's living with a relative

222
00:12:05,523 --> 00:12:08,151
so that she could stay on the team,
and keep playing.

223
00:12:08,734 --> 00:12:10,653
Do you know what it takes to do that?

224
00:12:10,736 --> 00:12:11,654
[girl] For sure.

225
00:12:11,737 --> 00:12:12,864
But Nagisa...

226
00:12:12,947 --> 00:12:14,907
I mean, I absolutely hear you.

227
00:12:14,991 --> 00:12:17,368
They're not gonna know
about any of that stuff,

228
00:12:17,452 --> 00:12:20,288
and it has nothing to do
with what happens on the court.

229
00:12:21,205 --> 00:12:24,792
But the fact is, I do know who she is
and what she's dealing with.

230
00:12:25,334 --> 00:12:26,878
I can't help being pissed off.

231
00:12:27,462 --> 00:12:29,380
So that's why she looked...

232
00:12:29,464 --> 00:12:31,132
[gloomy music playing]

233
00:12:32,592 --> 00:12:36,053
<i>Even Chinatsu
has to face her fair share of criticism.</i>

234
00:12:36,804 --> 00:12:38,639
<i>But I think she's perfect.</i>

235
00:12:39,307 --> 00:12:40,391
[exclaims]

236
00:12:41,601 --> 00:12:43,644
I don't want them to know we're here.

237
00:12:43,728 --> 00:12:45,354
What are you doing?

238
00:12:45,438 --> 00:12:47,398
Why not tell me
that you were standing there?

239
00:12:47,482 --> 00:12:49,484
I was spying on your spying, I guess?

240
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:50,776
[Taiki exclaims softly]

241
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:53,154
<i>Another adorable expression.</i>

242
00:12:53,237 --> 00:12:55,448
Yeah. I have awesome teammates.

243
00:12:56,741 --> 00:12:59,160
Come on, we have more windows to open.

244
00:12:59,243 --> 00:13:00,453
Yeah, yeah.

245
00:13:02,622 --> 00:13:03,664
I envy you.

246
00:13:03,748 --> 00:13:07,293
[Chinatsu] It's funny, Nagisa is acting
like it was her they were judging.

247
00:13:07,376 --> 00:13:09,420
Don't let that bother you.

248
00:13:09,504 --> 00:13:13,049
No matter what the other teams
might say about you,

249
00:13:13,132 --> 00:13:15,176
your team knows you work hard.

250
00:13:15,259 --> 00:13:17,303
And I know how much work you put in.

251
00:13:17,386 --> 00:13:19,430
- So don't let it--
- Nope. I let it bother me.

252
00:13:19,514 --> 00:13:20,431
Wha...

253
00:13:22,099 --> 00:13:25,186
[Chinatsu] I let it bother me,
and then I take them down.

254
00:13:25,811 --> 00:13:28,481
If I play well and lead my team
to beat Kagohara,

255
00:13:29,023 --> 00:13:31,442
then they'll never talk about me
like that again.

256
00:13:31,526 --> 00:13:32,610
[gasps softly]

257
00:13:34,529 --> 00:13:39,450
[Taiki] <i>Wow, she's hardcore,
the "rage in silence" type.</i>

258
00:13:40,284 --> 00:13:42,745
[Chinatsu] The fact is,
that's how Kagohara felt

259
00:13:42,828 --> 00:13:46,207
after watching me play,
so all I can do next time is...

260
00:13:48,209 --> 00:13:50,461
show them they made
the wrong call about me.

261
00:13:50,545 --> 00:13:51,671
[gasps]

262
00:13:52,797 --> 00:13:54,131
[uplifting music playing]

263
00:13:54,215 --> 00:13:55,716
[Taiki] <i>Man, she's cool.</i>

264
00:13:57,969 --> 00:14:01,722
<i>Chinatsu and Hina, they're both so cool.</i>

265
00:14:02,473 --> 00:14:05,726
<i>They both have their own way
of going after wins.</i>

266
00:14:15,778 --> 00:14:17,613
[coach] Semifinals tomorrow, people.

267
00:14:17,697 --> 00:14:19,574
{\an8}You can bet it'll be
more intense than today.

268
00:14:19,657 --> 00:14:20,616
{\an8}2 WINS TO NATIONALS

269
00:14:21,325 --> 00:14:23,494
- Keep your heads in the game!
- Yes, sir!

270
00:14:24,954 --> 00:14:25,872
[shuttlecock thuds]

271
00:14:25,955 --> 00:14:27,623
[all] Wow!

272
00:14:27,707 --> 00:14:28,875
It can't be.

273
00:14:28,958 --> 00:14:30,167
I can't believe this.

274
00:14:30,710 --> 00:14:32,587
[panting]

275
00:14:34,964 --> 00:14:36,382
[boy] Taiki just...

276
00:14:36,465 --> 00:14:38,301
[boy 2] Won a match against Haryu.

277
00:14:42,138 --> 00:14:44,640
[umpire] Second game, love all, play!

278
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:48,394
[Taiki] <i>The worst part about facing Haryu,</i>

279
00:14:48,477 --> 00:14:51,606
<i>is that he aims all his shots
where I least expect them.</i>

280
00:14:53,316 --> 00:14:54,150
[grunts]

281
00:14:54,775 --> 00:14:57,028
[Taiki] <i>When I think he'll drop
the shuttle near the net,</i>

282
00:14:57,111 --> 00:14:58,863
<i>the second I shift my weight
to move there,</i>

283
00:14:58,946 --> 00:15:00,698
<i>he sends it to my backcourt.</i>

284
00:15:00,781 --> 00:15:02,158
<i>And his form never changes,</i>

285
00:15:02,241 --> 00:15:05,411
<i>so I don't know where his shots
will go till the last moment.</i>

286
00:15:06,329 --> 00:15:09,415
<i>Which means,
I need to wait patiently before I move.</i>

287
00:15:10,082 --> 00:15:12,001
<i>Watch his racket closely.</i>

288
00:15:12,752 --> 00:15:13,669
[grunts]

289
00:15:13,753 --> 00:15:15,338
[thrilling music playing]

290
00:15:16,339 --> 00:15:17,173
[grunts]

291
00:15:17,924 --> 00:15:20,927
<i>Yes, I returned it!
Now to get back to center.</i>

292
00:15:21,010 --> 00:15:22,345
[grunts]

293
00:15:25,473 --> 00:15:26,390
[exclaims]

294
00:15:27,516 --> 00:15:29,060
Almost a close one.

295
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,521
I let my guard down.

296
00:15:34,148 --> 00:15:38,194
Until recently, you wouldn't
have been able to return that. [laughs]

297
00:15:38,945 --> 00:15:42,198
It's a good thing I figured that out
before the tournament.

298
00:15:47,787 --> 00:15:49,622
[shuttlecock thudding]

299
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:51,707
[grunts]

300
00:15:51,791 --> 00:15:55,002
Haryu completely flipped a switch
in the middle of the game.

301
00:15:55,086 --> 00:15:58,714
Yeah, there aren't many guys
who have a shot at competing with him.

302
00:15:58,798 --> 00:16:00,633
[boy 1] Taiki's gotten a lot better.

303
00:16:00,716 --> 00:16:04,720
It's obvious his speed has improved.
All that practice paid off.

304
00:16:04,804 --> 00:16:05,638
[Taiki grunts]

305
00:16:05,721 --> 00:16:09,976
[boy 2] Seeing this, it makes me feel like
anything could happen in the tournament.

306
00:16:10,059 --> 00:16:12,103
- [grunts]
- [whistle blows]

307
00:16:13,688 --> 00:16:16,232
Right, then, everyone.
It's time to head up.

308
00:16:16,315 --> 00:16:18,526
What? But things are getting good!

309
00:16:18,609 --> 00:16:20,987
[Coach Yuasa] I won't hear the end of it
if I let you stay.

310
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:22,863
Besides, if you keep at it,

311
00:16:22,947 --> 00:16:25,366
you'll tire yourselves out
before the tournament.

312
00:16:25,449 --> 00:16:27,368
You don't wanna be
out of juice on the last day.

313
00:16:27,451 --> 00:16:28,494
[Haryu] But, Coach!

314
00:16:28,577 --> 00:16:30,871
You two can just save it for the finals.

315
00:16:31,372 --> 00:16:33,874
Although, I don't know
when you'll face each other.

316
00:16:33,958 --> 00:16:35,042
[exclaims]

317
00:16:35,793 --> 00:16:37,128
[Haryu] There you have it.

318
00:16:38,004 --> 00:16:39,880
We'll have our rematch another day.

319
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:43,884
And so, until then, don't lose.

320
00:16:43,968 --> 00:16:45,094
[exclaims softly]

321
00:16:46,053 --> 00:16:46,887
Right!

322
00:16:47,471 --> 00:16:49,640
All righty, let's get this cleaned up!

323
00:16:49,724 --> 00:16:50,808
- On it.
- Yes!

324
00:17:01,235 --> 00:17:04,196
[Taiki] <i>Was I
holding my own against Haryu?</i>

325
00:17:12,997 --> 00:17:15,791
<i>I can score more points on him
than I used to.</i>

326
00:17:17,543 --> 00:17:21,172
<i>If I'm in good shape,
I just might be able to defeat him.</i>

327
00:17:21,756 --> 00:17:25,593
<i>Maybe take down Sajikawa,
and then make nationals.</i>

328
00:17:25,676 --> 00:17:26,594
Hey, Taiki.

329
00:17:28,304 --> 00:17:30,431
I've been wondering something for a while.

330
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:34,185
Will you confess to her
if you get to nationals?

331
00:17:35,311 --> 00:17:36,187
What?

332
00:17:36,270 --> 00:17:37,271
CONFESS

333
00:17:37,354 --> 00:17:38,522
I like you!

334
00:17:38,606 --> 00:17:39,690
[Chinatsu exclaims]

335
00:17:39,774 --> 00:17:41,942
MY FEELINGS

336
00:17:42,026 --> 00:17:43,194
{\an8}FOR

337
00:17:43,277 --> 00:17:45,196
{\an8}[Chinatsu] <i>I feel closer to you already.</i>

338
00:17:45,279 --> 00:17:46,113
{\an8}HER

339
00:17:46,197 --> 00:17:48,699
{\an8}<i>I wanna spend more time with you.</i>

340
00:17:48,783 --> 00:17:50,618
[church bells dinging]

341
00:17:51,243 --> 00:17:52,787
[exclaims in excitement]

342
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:54,830
[Kyo] You're jumping way ahead, dude.

343
00:17:56,290 --> 00:17:58,626
Looks like you're
more than ready to tell her.

344
00:17:58,709 --> 00:18:00,961
Well, actually,
that isn't the case at all.

345
00:18:01,754 --> 00:18:03,964
Of course I want to tell her
how I feel, but...

346
00:18:04,048 --> 00:18:06,425
I don't know, because what if she...

347
00:18:06,509 --> 00:18:09,595
What if I get rejected, and then she...

348
00:18:09,678 --> 00:18:12,473
doesn't feel comfortable
living at my house anymore?

349
00:18:13,015 --> 00:18:16,977
They say it's better to regret something
you've done than something you haven't.

350
00:18:17,812 --> 00:18:20,898
But I don't want to ignore
what she may be feeling,

351
00:18:20,981 --> 00:18:23,067
and push my feelings on her.

352
00:18:24,068 --> 00:18:25,486
Oh.

353
00:18:27,113 --> 00:18:29,907
- You're all grown up, huh?
- Oh! Shut up!

354
00:18:29,990 --> 00:18:31,784
- [Nishida] Taiki! Kyo!
- [Kyo] Hm?

355
00:18:32,576 --> 00:18:34,453
Wazzaaaa!

356
00:18:37,414 --> 00:18:39,625
- What's up?
- My dude, Yamamoto--

357
00:18:39,708 --> 00:18:41,377
It's Mr. Yamamoto.

358
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,880
He said he's gonna treat us
since we have a tournament coming up.

359
00:18:44,964 --> 00:18:46,632
Up to 500 yen a person.

360
00:18:46,715 --> 00:18:48,509
That was only meant for you two!

361
00:18:48,592 --> 00:18:50,136
[Kyo and Taiki] Why thank you!

362
00:18:50,219 --> 00:18:51,053
Hey!

363
00:18:51,846 --> 00:18:53,764
1,000 YEN

364
00:18:54,390 --> 00:18:56,016
Mr. Yamamoto's cool.

365
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:59,061
You would never catch Coach Yuasa
doing something nice like that.

366
00:18:59,145 --> 00:19:00,813
I wonder what we should buy.

367
00:19:04,859 --> 00:19:08,779
RESORT - TOP 10 BEACHES TO GO TO
LET'S GO TO THE BEACH!

368
00:19:09,989 --> 00:19:12,741
I would love to go
to the beach with Chinatsu.

369
00:19:12,825 --> 00:19:15,661
Isn't that just code for
"I wanna see her in a bikini?"

370
00:19:15,744 --> 00:19:16,662
Hey, Taiki.

371
00:19:17,246 --> 00:19:20,291
I wasn't trying to start up
that conversation again!

372
00:19:21,041 --> 00:19:24,545
I mean, there are a lot of places
I want to go with her, just the two of us.

373
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,798
But I gotta ask her out myself.

374
00:19:28,674 --> 00:19:30,509
{\an8}If I make it to nationals,

375
00:19:30,593 --> 00:19:33,053
{\an8}I feel like I've earned
the right to do that.

376
00:19:34,263 --> 00:19:35,848
- So...
- Hm.

377
00:19:37,391 --> 00:19:40,644
[Niina] The quiz had a question
on something you didn't even teach us.

378
00:19:40,728 --> 00:19:44,356
[Yamamoto] Had you used the workbook
I gave you at the start of the year,

379
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,567
you would've answered it quite easily.

380
00:19:46,650 --> 00:19:48,277
[Niina] What, like ages ago?

381
00:19:49,153 --> 00:19:50,487
[whimpers]

382
00:19:51,864 --> 00:19:53,115
Oops, forgot something.

383
00:19:53,657 --> 00:19:54,825
[gasps]

384
00:19:55,910 --> 00:19:56,911
[grunts]

385
00:19:58,913 --> 00:20:00,789
[Hina] You're eating something tasty.

386
00:20:02,666 --> 00:20:05,252
[Taiki] Hey! That's my fried chicken!

387
00:20:05,336 --> 00:20:06,462
[Hina] Mmm.

388
00:20:06,545 --> 00:20:08,339
Mr. Yamamoto paid, right?

389
00:20:08,422 --> 00:20:10,633
And you're watching calories, right?

390
00:20:10,716 --> 00:20:12,343
It's a good source of protein!

391
00:20:12,927 --> 00:20:14,220
Deep fried protein.

392
00:20:14,303 --> 00:20:16,472
Boy, are they comfortable with each other.

393
00:20:16,555 --> 00:20:19,350
You aren't kidding.
Their youth is blinding me.

394
00:20:19,433 --> 00:20:21,227
- [Hina] What?
- [Taiki groans]

395
00:20:21,310 --> 00:20:23,354
This is fried chicken we're talking about!

396
00:20:23,437 --> 00:20:25,606
[Hina] Okay, I get it, sheesh.

397
00:20:26,690 --> 00:20:29,652
On the last day,
I'll bring something nice for you.

398
00:20:30,194 --> 00:20:32,112
So you better stay in it till then!

399
00:20:33,239 --> 00:20:36,075
I'll make you the world-renowned
Hina Bento Box Special!

400
00:20:41,121 --> 00:20:44,875
[Taiki] <i>After that conversation,
I feel awkward looking her in the eye.</i>

401
00:20:45,501 --> 00:20:47,378
[Nagisa] So we get spending money or what?

402
00:20:47,461 --> 00:20:49,964
- And that's my cue!
- We're athletes, you know!

403
00:20:50,047 --> 00:20:50,881
Hey! Wait!

404
00:20:51,507 --> 00:20:54,718
Aren't you going to ask him
to treat you to something, Chinatsu?

405
00:20:54,802 --> 00:20:57,888
He said he couldn't afford
to treat any more students, so...

406
00:20:58,514 --> 00:21:00,516
can I have one?

407
00:21:01,225 --> 00:21:02,351
[exclaims softly]

408
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,772
- Of course.
- [Chinatsu exclaims]

409
00:21:07,731 --> 00:21:08,899
Thank you.

410
00:21:09,692 --> 00:21:11,652
[Taiki] <i>I didn't know she was a foodie.</i>

411
00:21:18,367 --> 00:21:20,411
Did you really want it that badly?

412
00:21:21,912 --> 00:21:22,830
[Chinatsu] Yeah.

413
00:21:25,124 --> 00:21:26,583
Seeing Hina ...

414
00:21:26,667 --> 00:21:28,794
it made me jealous.

415
00:21:30,421 --> 00:21:31,338
Huh?

416
00:21:36,552 --> 00:21:38,178
Thanks for sharing.

417
00:21:38,262 --> 00:21:41,432
Now I can really give my all
to my next game!

418
00:21:42,224 --> 00:21:43,600
[Nagisa] Chinatsu!

419
00:21:43,684 --> 00:21:44,643
Coming!

420
00:21:49,523 --> 00:21:54,445
[Taiki] <i>She meant she was jealous
about the fried chicken, right?</i>

421
00:21:59,116 --> 00:22:00,743
{\an8}<i>Or maybe...</i>

422
00:22:05,539 --> 00:22:07,541
[closing theme song playing]
